WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.034
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.034 --> 00:00:03.136
My name is Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.537
And these are the Roots,
right there.

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.473
-Whoo!
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:09.542
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.210
Well, guys, everyone
is still buzzing

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.179
about Joe Biden
picking Kamala Harris

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.514
as his running mate.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.982
It looks like they didn't
waste any time

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.383
hitting the campaign trail.

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:19.786 line:0%
-Tonight the new
2020 Democrat ticket

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:22.722 line:0%
making its debut.
Joe Biden and Kamala Harris

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.724 line:0%
appearing together
for the first time

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:27.260 line:0%
since she was selected
as his running mate.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.030
-That's right, Biden and Harris
shared the stage

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.931
for the first time
since the debates.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.666
You can tell Biden
hasn't forgotten,

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:36.169
'cause when Harris went in
for a handshake, he flinched.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:38.371
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:41.607
Yep, Biden and Harris appeared
at a high school in Delaware.

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:43.209
As soon as he heard that,
Trump was like,

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.545
"I'm closing all schools
immediately."

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.246
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:49.748
That's right, today's event
was in Wilmington, Delaware,

00:00:49.748 --> 00:00:52.117
which is timely because
the city's official motto

00:00:52.117 --> 00:00:55.555
is actually, "Wilmington -- the
Zoom meeting room of cities."

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:58.757
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.757 --> 00:01:00.893
As of right now,
Biden and Harris

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:03.362
are up by 10 points
on Trump and Pence.

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:05.398
Just to rub it in,
at the end of their event,

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.000
they both moonwalked
down a ramp.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.568
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.568 --> 00:01:11.871
Of course, once Joe Biden
announced Kamala Harris

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.306
as his running mate,
Trump couldn't wait to weigh in.

00:01:14.306 --> 00:01:15.908
Here's what he had to say
about Harris

00:01:15.908 --> 00:01:17.309
at a press conference
last night.

00:01:17.309 --> 00:01:19.211
-She was very, very nasty.

00:01:19.211 --> 00:01:21.814
She was very disrespectful
to Joe Biden.

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:26.085
And it's hard to pick somebody
that's that disrespectful.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:27.754
-Yeah, unfortunately for Harris,

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.755
if you want well-wishes
from Trump,

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:31.090
you got to be in prison.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.793
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:36.862
Meanwhile, in a new attack ad,
the Trump campaign

00:01:36.862 --> 00:01:40.066
has already labeled them
Slow Joe and Phony Kamala.

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:42.102 line:0%
And if you have
a slow-and-phony joke

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:44.270 line:0%
that doesn't end with,
"Those used to be

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.439 line:0%
Trump's nicknames
for Eric and Don Jr.,"

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.374 line:0%
write to us at
the Tonight Show Writers,

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:52.678 line:0%
30 Rockefeller Plaza,
New York, New York 10112.

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:54.413
And it's not just Trump
on the attack.

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:56.415
While speaking to a crowd
in Arizona yesterday,

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:58.851
Mike Pence welcomed Harris
to the race.

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:00.320
Listen to this.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.223
-Let me take this opportunity
to welcome her to the race.

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:05.859
Y'all might like to know that
the vice presidential debate

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:09.395
is gonna be held
on October 7th in Utah.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:12.231
So my message to the Democratic
candidate for vice president?

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:15.167
[ Laughter ]
Congratulations.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:17.403
I'll see you in Salt Lake City.

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:20.339
[ Laughter ]
-Ew!

00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:23.209
Ew!

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.077
-I'm pretty sure
that's the first time

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:26.912
a guy has tried
to intimidate someone

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:29.282
with the phrase, "I'll see you
in Salt Lake City."

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:32.418
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.019
Never hear Joker tell Batman,

00:02:34.019 --> 00:02:36.288
"And we're gonna settle this...

00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:37.590
in Salt Lake City!"

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.426
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.795
My Joker sounds
like Richard Dreyfuss.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:43.929
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.929 --> 00:02:46.432
"We're gonna settle this
in Salt Lake City!"

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:49.702
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.771
"Mr. Holland's Opus" --
no, I can't.

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:54.640
-Wait. How long did it take you
to work on that?

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.310
-That was what I thought
the Joker sounded like.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.312
[ Laughter ]
I don't know.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:03.116
"And we'll settle this
in Salt Lake City!"

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:05.117
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:06.885
-That's spot-on!
-No.

00:03:06.885 --> 00:03:09.655
The vice presidential debate
is in Utah?

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:12.625
Man, talk about a home-field
advantage for Pence, huh?

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.627
That's a lucky break.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.763
It's like it's being called back
to the white mothership.

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:19.332
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:21.334
Feels like the election
is really started,

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.102
now that Joe Biden
and Kamala Harris

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.903
have hit the campaign trail
together.

00:03:24.903 --> 00:03:26.238
Well, I guess, to compete

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:28.241
with all the attention
their appearance was getting,

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:31.044
Trump held his own address.
Take a look at this.

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:33.179
-Welcome, everyone,
to this very exciting,

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:35.348
very -- everyone's
very excited about this.

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.183
Look at Mike Pence.
He's very excited.

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:38.351
Everyone's excited.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.152
Me and Mike are in the league,

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:42.622
and that's -- I'm -- I'm being
told that's a good thing.

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.057
It's a very good thing.

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:46.259
Mike's got what it takes.
Kamala, though --

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:48.293
Kamala didn't do well
in the primary,

00:03:48.293 --> 00:03:49.996
as we all remember.
[ Sniffs ]

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:53.299
In fact, she was destroyed by
the much fiercer candidate --

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:56.568
a candidate I wouldn't want
to go up against -- Joe Biden.

00:03:56.568 --> 00:03:58.971
He was very good against her.
Very good.

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:01.006
But, look, Joe Biden
is very weak.

00:04:01.006 --> 00:04:03.142
And, look, anyone
could take him down.

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:06.145
Kamala could take him down.
She did very well against him

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:07.747
in the debates.
It's true.

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.682
Mike and I can't wait
to get out there.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:12.951
We're campaigning everywhere,
from Yo-Semite National Park

00:04:12.951 --> 00:04:16.222
to the banks of the mighty
Miss-Pee-Pee River,

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:19.759
to all the canyons --
Grand Canyon.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:22.261
It's a very grand canyon,
Grand Cayman.

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:27.166
All the canyons and the Caymans
and the crayons.

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.667
People are calling me, saying,

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.570
"I've never seen
crayons like this.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:33.906
Look at the colors --
indigo and maize.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.975
Do they still have maize?

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:39.111
I always thought periwinkle
was an odd choice, periwinkle.

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:41.581
I would have called it
"light purple."

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.615
"Lurple."

00:04:43.615 --> 00:04:45.752
Can we look into "lurple"?

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.253
Mike's gonna look into "lurple."

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:49.621
Y-You won't get lurple
with Kamala, folks.

00:04:49.621 --> 00:04:50.856
You won't get lurple.

00:04:50.856 --> 00:04:53.959
Unfair, [Sniffs] nasty,

00:04:53.959 --> 00:04:56.562
[Sniffs] sleepy, [Sniffs]

00:04:56.562 --> 00:05:00.333
phony, [Sniffs], unfair,
[Sniffs] nasty,

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.634
[Sniffs] sleepy, [Sniffs]
phony [Sniffs].

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:02.868
Ah-choo!

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.870
But we're gonna win every state
in November --

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:07.673
California, New York,
beautiful Thigh-land.

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:09.508
I love Thigh-land.

00:05:09.508 --> 00:05:11.144
Has a beautiful capital --

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:12.911
earmuffs --

00:05:12.911 --> 00:05:14.914
Bangkok.

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:17.517
I didn't want you to hear
"Bangkok."

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:19.418
Anyway, folks,
that's enough from me.

00:05:19.418 --> 00:05:21.753
I think it's time we heard
from the man himself.

00:05:21.753 --> 00:05:24.123
Mike, the floor is yours.

00:05:27.693 --> 00:05:29.595
-Ew. Hope he's okay.

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:31.197
Yeah, Trump is everywhere.

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:33.065
Last night, he called in
to Fox News

00:05:33.065 --> 00:05:35.067
to chat with Sean Hannity.
At one point,

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:37.336
he started complaining
about mail-in voting.

00:05:37.336 --> 00:05:38.538
Listen to what he said.

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:40.639 line:0%
-This whole thing
with this mail-in ballot,

00:05:40.639 --> 00:05:43.108 line:0%
that's a rigged election
waiting to happen.

00:05:43.108 --> 00:05:45.211 line:0%
It's rigged, and
everyone knows it.

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:48.447 line:0%
Because you can't send out
60 million mail-in ballots.

00:05:48.447 --> 00:05:52.051 line:0%
Who knows who's getting them?
The mailmen are gonna get them,

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:54.920 line:0%
and people are just gonna
grab batches of them.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.856 line:0%
And you talk about China
and Russia,

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:58.724 line:0%
they'll be grabbing
plenty of them.

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:01.794
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.764 --> 00:06:06.899
Usually -- Usually,
when an old man

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:09.435
starts accusing people
of stealing the mail,

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:11.771
it's time to put Grandpa down
for his nap.

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:13.206
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:15.074
I guess, three months from now,
the Russians will be like,

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:17.710
"Ugh, so many
Pottery Barn catalogs.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.378
Why do we keep sending?

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:21.747
Oh, that's a good deal."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.747 --> 00:06:23.616
Trump turned into that guy
who calls in

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:25.384
to a sports radio show
every morning,

00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:27.286
and the host can't get him
off the line.

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:29.522
He's like, "[Chuckles]
Alright, okay, Chuck, okay.

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:31.090
We got to take another call.
Alright.

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:34.059
Hey, focus on driving, Chuck."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.059 --> 00:06:35.761
Well, guys,
one of the big things

00:06:35.761 --> 00:06:37.396
everyone's talking about
right now

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:38.697
is reopening of schools.

00:06:38.697 --> 00:06:41.834
And I heard that contact tracing
will be a big part

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:43.769
or reducing COVID in classrooms.

00:06:43.769 --> 00:06:46.072 line:0%
Here to comment is
East Ridge County eighth grader

00:06:46.072 --> 00:06:48.473 line:0%
Riley Spellman.
Hi, Riley.

00:06:48.473 --> 00:06:50.543 line:0%
Thank you for being here.

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:52.578 line:0%
So, you're starting up school
in the fall.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.847 line:0%
DO you think contact tracing
will actually work?

00:06:54.847 --> 00:06:57.549 line:0%
-Oh, for sure, Jimmy.
I'm not worried.

00:06:57.549 --> 00:06:59.819 line:0%
-Okay, I got it.
Well, I thought it'd be fun

00:06:59.819 --> 00:07:03.288 line:0%
if we just practiced
maybe a little right now.

00:07:03.288 --> 00:07:05.458 line:0%
So, Riley,
other than your family,

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:08.260 line:0%
can you tell us
who you've been in contact with

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.361 line:0%
in the last week?

00:07:09.361 --> 00:07:12.164 line:0%
-No one. Just my family.

00:07:12.164 --> 00:07:15.001 line:0%
-Really? That's great.

00:07:15.001 --> 00:07:18.637 line:0%
I guess that shows how easy --
-Oh, and Ashley M.

00:07:18.637 --> 00:07:21.707 line:0%
-Oh, Ashley M. Okay.
-But she doesn't count.

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:24.777 line:0%
She's my BFF, so she's
basically like family.

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:27.513 line:0%
-Well, no, actually,
technically, she's not family.

00:07:27.513 --> 00:07:29.615 line:0%
But that's fine.
So all we have to do

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:32.284 line:0%
for contact tracing
is call Ashley M.,

00:07:32.284 --> 00:07:33.552 line:0%
and we'd be good.

00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:35.588 line:0%
-Although I saw
on Ashley M.'s finsta

00:07:35.588 --> 00:07:37.590 line:0%
that she got froyo
with Brian L.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.325 line:0%
-Got froyo. Okay. Well, okay.

00:07:39.325 --> 00:07:42.128 line:0%
-And I know he saw Emma R. --
not the one from our school,

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:43.729 line:0%
the one from
Southbrook Middle --

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:45.631 line:0%
because they a TikTok together.

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:47.933 line:0%
And, TPH, it was cringe.

00:07:47.933 --> 00:07:50.803 line:0%
Plus, Emma went to the park
with Cooper.

00:07:50.803 --> 00:07:52.905 line:0%
I mean, they wore masks, obs.

00:07:52.905 --> 00:07:55.441 line:0%
But Cooper does
this really funny thing

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:58.577 line:0%
where he puts his mask
over his chest like a bra.

00:07:58.577 --> 00:08:00.980 line:0%
So I think that counts
as contact.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:04.149 line:0%
-Uh, y-yeah, that
definitely does count.

00:08:04.149 --> 00:08:05.951 line:0%
Is -- Is that it, right there?

00:08:05.951 --> 00:08:08.120 line:0%
-Yes. Actually, no.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:11.423 line:0%
Because Cooper and Kiley
for sure hung out,

00:08:11.423 --> 00:08:14.292 line:0%
because, high-key, she told me
she wants to get with him

00:08:14.292 --> 00:08:15.561 line:0%
before school starts.

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:18.130 line:0%
Problem is, Kiley
is still dating Dustin,

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:20.599 line:0%
whose brother licks poles.
-Uh, what?

00:08:20.599 --> 00:08:24.536 line:0%
-And so Dustin is, "Y'okay,"
that Kiley wants to H.U. Cooper.

00:08:24.536 --> 00:08:26.305 line:0%
Anyway, I'm sure
none of this matters.

00:08:26.305 --> 00:08:28.240 line:0%
But -- ugh -- sorry
for the tea overload.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:31.410 line:0%
But, like, yeah. [ Chuckles ]

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:32.744 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:08:32.744 --> 00:08:35.014 line:0%
-Um, a-actually,
all of this matters, Riley,

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:38.384 line:0%
because this is
what contact tracing is.

00:08:38.384 --> 00:08:41.286 line:0%
-Ohhh.

00:08:41.286 --> 00:08:44.657 line:0%
Well, yeah,
this will never work.

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:47.559 line:0%
-Riley Spellman, everyone.
Uh, put your hands together.

00:08:47.559 --> 00:08:50.996 line:0%
-I don't think that's enough.
-And it still counts. Just...

00:08:50.996 --> 00:08:54.166
Let's get to some business news,
everyone.

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:56.769
I saw that Burger King
is now making face masks

00:08:56.769 --> 00:08:59.137
with orders printed on them,
so that...

00:08:59.137 --> 00:09:00.506
[ Laughs ]

00:09:00.506 --> 00:09:03.408
So that customers
don't have to speak.

00:09:03.408 --> 00:09:04.577 line:0%
Check this. Look at these.

00:09:04.577 --> 00:09:06.479 line:0%
That's to order, right there,
yeah.

00:09:06.479 --> 00:09:07.580 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.348 line:0%
Maybe Burger King
is onto something.

00:09:09.348 --> 00:09:12.218 line:0%
Unfortunately, it doesn't quite
work as well as CVS --

00:09:12.218 --> 00:09:14.587 line:0%
"hemorrhoid cream
and wart remover."

00:09:14.587 --> 00:09:17.756 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:09:17.756 --> 00:09:19.558
And finally --
this is pretty funny --

00:09:19.558 --> 00:09:21.727 line:0%
a Tennessee woman received
her driver's license

00:09:21.727 --> 00:09:23.762 line:0%
with just a picture
of an empty chair.

00:09:23.762 --> 00:09:27.266 line:0%
Take a look at this.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:27.266 --> 00:09:28.801
Meanwhile, the chair
saw the photo

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:30.369
and was like, "Damn it!
I blinked!"

00:09:30.369 --> 00:09:32.170
[ Laughter ]
The good news is,

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:34.106
if she gets pulled over,
she can just ditch the car

00:09:34.106 --> 00:09:36.208
and leave her license
on the seat.

